{
 "_schema": "phantasie.creation-tables/v1",
 "_source": "Phantasie III, DOS SSI 1988 (reverse-engineering/dos/phantasie3/extracted/, FORMAT.md): MAIN.EXE DGROUP tables (extracted/rule-tables.json, tools/scripts/extract_dos_p3_rules.py) and the III manual",
 "_note": "Keys are Core's class / race names (Phantasie I order). hp_factors = III's HP dice for levels 1-15 (DS:0xa78) [C] (L16-22 in rule-tables.json); mp_ceiling = DS:0xafb [C], cell for cell the manual's Maximum Magic Points table (III PDF 10 / pr.14); skill_coefficients = III's eight class tables in I's slot layout [C]; spell_levels = DS:0x1208 [C] bytes, = the manual's Spells Available table cell for cell (index = spell number - 1, 57 entries). class / race attribute modifiers and ceilings: the III manual's tables (III PDF 4 / pr.3), which are Phantasie I's manual tables value for value (09-trilogy-manual-p3.md 1a), copied from GameData/phantasie1 (manual values, D-001 applied); DOS III's own tables are static data in MAIN.EXE [C] (s88, FORMAT.md section 4.3) and match these except Kobold CHA max (DOS 3, manual 13: D3-034). lifespan_bands: D3-041 (user s99, manual): III's manual has I's lifespan text word for word, so I's D-003 bands apply (manual figure +-10 %, picked by LCK 8..13); DOS III writes a maximum age but never reads it (the p3.lifespans dos option).",
 "_skill_tables_vs_I": "III's skill tables equal Phantasie I's TWNS.INT tables except five cells, kept as read: Thief Pick Lock L3 35 (I 55), Ranger Attack L15 25 (I 250), Ranger Parry L15 60 (I 85), and Monk / Wizard Parry read one level ahead of I's rows (III's Parry table is one byte short after Ranger L14, so Monk L15 = 40 and Wizard L15 = 0) [C] bytes.",
